1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,539
Each modal carries several meanings.

2
00:00:02,539 --> 00:00:07,096
Can: ability, informal permission, general possibility.

3
00:00:07,096 --> 00:00:10,533
Could: past ability and polite requests.

4
00:00:10,533 --> 00:00:15,078
May: formal permission, or about fifty per cent possibility.

5
00:00:15,078 --> 00:00:17,382
Might: a weaker possibility.

6
00:00:17,382 --> 00:00:20,768
Will: future, willingness, promise.

7
00:00:20,768 --> 00:00:26,002
Would: polite offers, past habits and unreal situations.

8
00:00:26,002 --> 00:00:29,075
Shall: offers and suggestions with I and we.

9
00:00:29,075 --> 00:00:30,403
Should: advice.

10
00:00:30,403 --> 00:00:34,505
Must: strong obligation, or a confident deduction.

11
00:00:34,505 --> 00:00:42,148
So the safe method in the exam: read the whole sentence, name the meaning you need, and only then choose the word.

